// the other way to check a leak, and the only one that can see the state *after* the program's own
// module-scope teardown: --explain-memory, which has `main` print what is outstanding on its way out
//
// `$c` is released after the last statement of this file, so `mem::live_allocations()` written here would
// still count it. the report is emitted past that point, which is what makes it the whole-program answer
class Counter
{
    int32 $value;
}

Counter $c = Counter(7);
echo $c->value;

array<int32> $numbers = [1, 2, 3];
$numbers->push(4);
echo $numbers[3];
